1. SETTINGS GEAR / HOME PAGE TOP HUD

The Settings interface itself is now much better. Do not redesign it again unless there is a functional problem.

The remaining issue is the Settings gear position.

The gear needs to be in the TRUE upper-left corner of the Home Page.

I suspect the reason this has not been fixed is that the top HUD already occupies the highest area, including:
- Champion/title
- Level
- Tower indicator
- XP gauge
- XP amount/counter
- XP label
- Other top HUD elements

Do NOT move the Settings gear downward.

Instead:
- Keep the Settings gear independently anchored to the true upper-left corner.
- Move the other top HUD elements slightly downward as necessary.
- Lower the Champion/Level area.
- Lower the Tower indicator.
- Lower the XP gauge.
- Lower the XP counter/XP label.
- Reorganize the top HUD if necessary to create enough space.
- Keep the gear separated from the HUD.
- Make it responsive on desktop and mobile.

The intended hierarchy is:
Settings gear = true upper-left corner
Other HUD elements = slightly below it.

2. TUTORIAL SPOTLIGHT

The tutorial is now much better and no longer gets permanently stuck, so do NOT rebuild it from scratch.

Currently, the target receives a golden frame, but it is not actually illuminated.

Improve it so:
- Everything outside the current target is dimmed.
- The target remains bright/clearly visible.
- Add a subtle glow/spotlight effect around the target.
- The player should immediately understand what they need to click/touch.
- The gold frame can remain, but it should accompany the spotlight rather than replace it.
- Make it work on desktop and mobile.

3. SIMPLIFY THE INITIAL TUTORIAL

The current tutorial teaches too many unrelated systems.

It currently goes roughly:
Continue button → Lessons → Tower → Shop → Leaderboard → Achievements → Lucky Wheel/Word of the Day → etc.

This is unnecessary.

The initial tutorial should teach the actual gameplay/learning loop.

The first important instruction can be:
“This is the Continue button. Click/touch it to enter your current lesson.”

After the player clicks it, the tutorial should follow the actual progression.

Do NOT give the player a tutorial tour of:
- Tower tab
- Shop
- Leaderboards
- Achievements
- Other unrelated navigation tabs

The strange Shop → Leaderboard → Achievements sequence should be removed.

Those systems can be discovered later when relevant.

The first tutorial should focus on:
Home → Continue Your Journey → Lesson → Test/Gameplay → Minions → Boss → progression.

4. CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY / LESSON PROGRESSION

Continue Your Journey now correctly opens the current lesson. Keep that.

However, the progression is currently:

Lesson 1 → Lesson 2 → Lesson 3 → Go to Tower → first battle

That is NOT the intended structure.

Do not force the player to complete all three free lessons consecutively before any gameplay.

We need meaningful checkpoints:

Lesson content → Test/checkpoint → Regular enemies/minions → Boss → next progression.

Inspect the existing project structure and previous implementation to determine the intended relationships. Do not invent an arbitrary system.

